[stderr] ### PROJECT_BRIEF.md
[stderr] # Product brief — football-trivia-e2e
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Source of truth:** [`INITIAL.md`](INITIAL.md). This normalized brief preserves
[stderr] its scope; it records unknowns and contradictions instead of choosing them.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Problem, category, users, and outcome
[stderr] 
[stderr] Casual adult football followers need a satisfying way to test and extend their
[stderr] knowledge in a few mobile-friendly minutes. This is an original 2D,
[stderr] single-player football-trivia puzzle with themed rounds, varied question
[stderr] formats, answer validation, score/streak feedback, local progress, and a
[stderr] curated question bank.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The first useful session succeeds when a player completes an onboarding round,
[stderr] understands accepted/rejected feedback and score/streak, then saves and resumes.
[stderr] This is the quiz equivalent of the source's generic “first battle” text; a
[stderr] literal battle/campaign is a decision, not assumed scope.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## First-release and roadmap scope
[stderr] 
[stderr] First release: playable themed rounds; tutorial; question formats and answer
[stderr] rules; accessible feedback; scoring/streaks; anti-repetition; local
[stderr] progress/save/load/resume/recovery; settings/accessibility; original
[stderr] audio/visual feedback; curated, reviewed, versioned question content; content
[stderr] delivery; and crash/error recovery. Named account/identity, multiplayer safety,
[stderr] live operations, and purchases are decision-gated, not automatic dependencies.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Success is measurable when a new player can complete onboarding, play an
[stderr] authored round, get deterministic answer/score feedback, save and restore
[stderr] confirmed progress, and recover from interruption or a safe update without
[stderr] silent loss on every selected target. Every shipped question has category,
[stderr] format, answer rule, difficulty, provenance/review record, and repeat-eligibility
[stderr] metadata. Bank size, completion cadence, and performance thresholds are open.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Deferred: live/seasonal events, player-created/shared content, advanced
[stderr] analytics, and advanced monetisation. Non-goals: copied branding, assets,
[stderr] questions/copy, layouts, or distinctive interactions; and unapproved RPG world,
[stderr] party, quest, combat, boss, or literal battle systems.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Target systems
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Target | First-release role | Input model | Delivery constraint | Out of scope |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Responsive web app | Full shared game on phone, tablet, desktop. | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad. | Responsive compatibility and performance budget to be approved. | Separate web ruleset/campaign. |
[stderr] | PWA | Installable form of the same game. | Supported browser/device inputs. | Offline content/saves and safe cache refresh that protects confirmed progress. | Always-online dependency or PWA-only mode. |
[stderr] | Android phone | Compatible packaged mobile delivery of shared core. | Touch; orientation undecided. | Battery, thermal, size, privacy, packaging, store rules. | Android-exclusive game content. |
[stderr] | iPhone (iOS) | Compatible packaged mobile delivery of shared core. | Touch; orientation undecided. | Battery, thermal, size, privacy, packaging, store rules. | iOS-exclusive game content. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Use a shared core with necessary platform adaptations only. Remote
[stderr] account-linked state may use a safe local cache where approved, and must not
[stderr] silently discard confirmed single-player progress.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Constraints, assumptions, and reference boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] Explicit constraints: accessible controls/text/captions/visual settings;
[stderr] save/resume/data-loss recovery; crash reporting/player recovery; web/PWA plus
[stderr] Android/iOS; feasible slow-network behaviour; localisation/privacy/platform
[stderr] requirements; and original expression. Safe assumptions: independently authored
[stderr] content/UI/art/audio; editorial fact review; locally available approved content
[stderr] supports a basic session; outages are clear; and diagnostics minimise personal
[stderr] data. No stack, vendor, backend, account, retention, or licensing choice is
[stderr] approved by these assumptions.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Reference | Allowed functional learning | Prohibited |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | The Athletic | Football-topic breadth and varied quiz formats. | Brand, questions/copy, assets, layouts, editorial structure, screens, and interactions. |
[stderr] | QuizUp | Broad goal of short competitive-feeling trivia sessions. | Brand, questions/copy, assets, layouts, flows, social systems, and interaction choreography. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Human approval decisions
[stderr] 
[stderr] 1. Is generic “story/campaign” and “first battle” text real scope, or should a
[stderr]    lightweight themed quiz journey replace it?
[stderr] 2. For account identity, multiplayer safety, live operations, and purchases:
[stderr]    choose release-critical, optional connected enhancement, or deferred.
[stderr] 3. Decide account/authentication, sync/conflicts, retention/deletion, recovery,
[stderr]    outage, safety/moderation, age/region, refund/entitlement policies if any
[stderr]    connected or commerce feature ships.
[stderr] 4. Choose delivery approach, OS/browser/device matrix, orientation, budgets,
[stderr]    update/crash provider/cost model, and Android/iOS packaging path.
[stderr] 5. Approve question-bank size, coverage, source/licensing/provenance, refresh,
[stderr]    adjudication, languages, and exact accessibility/audio scope.
